      <rules>
        <rule name="Drone Squadron" id="fac1-5925-95ec-e8e0" hidden="false">
          <description>During deployment, models in this unit do not have to be placed within control range of each other and can be grouped with different units. As soon as this unit is deployed, each model is treated as a separate unit until the end of the battle.
Models in this unit cannot contest or claim any objective markers and do not accrue attrition points, and no abilities are triggered, nor victory points scored, when they are destroyed.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Priority Target - Command action" id="83f2-b397-6ced-c72b" hidden="false">
          <description>During the Strategy Phase, one unit with this ability can make this action.
Select one unit visible to any Seeker or Pathfinder models on the battlefield as a priority target. Until the end of the turn, the following effects apply to all friendly Seeker or Pathfinder models on the battlefield, and any units grouped with them:
* The priority target does not benefit from cover while this unit is within 12” of it.
* When this unit wishes to react to the priority target, add 2 to its Initiative.
Only one friendly unit may make this action each turn.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Auri" typeId="cost-auri" value="95"/>
      </costs>
