  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Ranked Fire" id="ae07-7486-20a6-2acb" hidden="false">
      <description>If all models in this unit are in base lock, when a model in this unit targets an enemy unit with its ranged weapons within 12”, it may reroll natural attack rolls of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explosive End (D5”)" id="ed1f-a2b1-977b-a80d" hidden="false">
      <description>When this unit is destroyed, before removing the model, it explodes in a D5” blast radius from its base, with a strength of +3 and a damage of 1. If this unit had *altitude* when it was destroyed, the explosion has strength of +5 and a damage of 3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aethercraft" id="8e65-6439-1495-6995" hidden="false">
      <description>During deployment, or when this unit is activated in the movement phase, if it has not been successfully charged that turn, it can choose to gain or lose the *altitude* keyword. An *altitude* unit is subject to the following:
* Add 10 to an *altitude* unit’s speed characteristic.
* This unit has disadvantage when targeting non-*altitude* units.
* This unit cannot be affected by any *aura* abilities, enemy invocations, or any blast radii or attacks that select a point or area on the battlefield.
* This unit cannot make charges.
* This unit cannot contest objectives.
All non-*altitude* units have *vertical disadvantage*. A unit with vertical disadvantage:
* Always has disadvantage on attacks targeting *altitude* units, regardless of any abilities which would give it advantage (such as advantage against *vehicle* or *airborne* units).
* Cannot target *altitude* units with melee weapons or weapons with a limited range.
* Cannot charge *altitude* units. Additionally, altitude units never count as the closest unit for the purposes of disordered charges.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grand Admiral of the Aventine Fleets" id="b529-7c22-65df-2744" hidden="false">
      <description>Your force may only ever include one *Fleetmaster* unit, and if your force includes one, it is always your *warlord*, superseding all other options.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skatecraft" id="1958-255b-b7e3-5d3e" hidden="false">
      <description>Each time this unit makes an advance move, it can move up to its full Speed characteristic instead of only half.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explosive End (Skatecraft, D5”)" id="03f2-d152-4f9e-2998" hidden="false">
      <description>When this unit is destroyed, before removing the model, roll a dice. On a 5+, it explodes in a *blast* attack, with a D5” radius originating from its base, with a strength of +3 and a damage of 1. If this unit made an advance move in the turn in which it was destroyed, the explosion has strength of +5 and a damage of 3.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
